  "slug": "simulations-structural-6310",
  "summary": "MD-based benchmarking and AlphaFold3 ensemble tests now probe dynamics beyond single static predictions across motifs, loops and peptides.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is a shift from single static structures toward dynamics and conformational ensembles as the basis for judging structural models. BILBY-MD all-atom MD evaluation of 220 PROSITE-derived motif scaffolds indicates that static refolding success overstates dynamical fidelity. AlphaFold3 pseudo-ensembles are tested for parallel versus antiparallel beta-sheet organization and polymorphism in short amyloidogenic peptides. Gly/Pro enrichment and flexibility in six-residue Omega-loops are linked to interface-dependent conservation across protein complexes. A PyTorch reimplementation of local energetic frustration analysis reports near-identical results to FrustratometeR at 70-13,000x GPU speedups, enabling proteome-scale analysis. What is new is the explicit dynamics-aware benchmarking of motif scaffolds, while the remaining work contributes ensemble, flexibility and frustration analyses rather than a single shared method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
